●	Title: Calculate vegetation and water/ soil indices 
●	Procedure: 
●	1. Perform the NDVI and NDWI computation in QGIS using Raster Calculator.  
●	Part (a) Calculate NDVI using the MODIS bands shared with you. (You can also use  LISS3 data's NIR & RED bands)  
●	Part (b) Calculate NDWI using B3.tif and B5.tif, in QGIS. Both bands correspond to the Landsat 8 
satellite image.  
NDVI Calculation 
1.	Open QGIS and create a new project. 
2.	Go to Layer → Add Layer → Add Raster Layer and load the required bands (MODIS.RED, MODIS.NIR, 
B3.tif, B5.tif). 
3.	Open Raster → Raster Calculator. 
4.	From the Raster Bands list, double-click the NIR band and Red band to form the NDVI expression. Don't add space in the formula. 
[.("MODIS_18Dec17_NIR@1" - "MODIS_18Dec17_RED@1") / 
("MODIS_18Dec17_NIR@1" + "MODIS_18Dec17_RED@1") ] 
5.	Click the … (three dots) button next to the Output layer. 
6.	Choose Save to File and name it NDVI.tif. 
7.	Click OK to run the process. 
8.	After the output is generated, right-click the NDVI layer → Properties → Symbology. 
9.	Change render type to Singleband pseudocolor and apply a suitable color ramp.(Green for NDVI). 
  
NDWI Calculation(Same as NDVI) 
1.	From the Raster Bands list, double-click the Green band (B3) and NIR band (B5). 
  
2.	Choose Save to File and name it NDWI.tif. 
3.	Click OK to run the process. 
4.	Select Singleband pseudocolor and apply an appropriate color ramp(Blue for NDWI) 
  






